4110 {\cf20 // Provides a multilane implementation of an atomic variable that supports add, sub, load,}\par
4111 {\cf20 // store. Instead of using a single atomic variable, this splits up into multiple ones,}\par
4112 {\cf20 // each sitting on a separate cache line. The goal is to provide a speedup when most}\par
4113 {\cf20 // operations are modifying. It achieves this with two properties:}\par
4114 {\cf20 //}\par
4115 {\cf20 // * Multiple atomics are used, so chance of congestion from the same atomic is reduced.}\par
4116 {\cf20 // * Each atomic sits on a separate cache line, so false sharing is reduced.}\par
4117 {\cf20 //}\par
4118 {\cf20 // The disadvantage is that there is a small overhead due to the use of TLS, and load/store}\par
4119 {\cf20 // is slower because all atomics have to be accessed.}\par
4120 {\cf17 template} <{\cf17 typename} T>\par
4121 {\cf17 class }MultiLaneAtomic \{\par
4122     {\cf17 struct }CacheLineAlignedAtomic \{\par
